# meta::genre = interview
# meta::salientEntities = 2 (5*), 3 (5*), 4 (5*), 5 (5*), 13 (4*), 1 (3*), 43 (3), 10 (2), 69 (2), 7 (1), 8 (1), 12 (1), 14 (1), 15 (1), 16 (1), 39 (1), 41 (1), 47 (1), 49 (1), 50 (1), 51 (1), 52 (1), 53 (1), 61 (1), 67 (1), 70 (1), 71 (1)
# meta::sourceURL = https://en.wikinews.org/wiki/Wikinews_interviews_Mario_J._Lucero_and_Isabel_Ruiz_of_Heaven_Sent_Gaming
# meta::speakerCount = 3
# meta::summary1 = (human1) In an interview with Wikinews, Mario J. Lucero and Isabel Ruiz, who run a website called Heaven Sent Gaming, talk about how they met in school, the people involved in their project and the motivation for their work.
# meta::summary2 = (human2) Wikinews interviews Mario J Lucero and Isabel Ruiz about how they formed Heaven Sent Gaming, and they discussed how they met in high school and then went to college together in Arizona, where they worked together on class projects by combining Mario’s writing with Isabel’s drawings.
# meta::summary3 = (human3) Mario Lucero and Isabel Ruiz talk about their gaming company, Heaven Sent Gaming, mentioning some of the early projects they worked on in high school and college, such as comics and drawings and describing how their mission is to bring light to the entertainment and media industry, citing a bible verse.
# meta::summary4 = (human4) Mario J. Lucero and Isabel Ruiz explain to Wikinews how they met in high school and what led to their “entertainment team”, Heaven Sent Gaming, and their various projects such as the comic Karis and the story Thad’s World Destruction, while working with other colleagues and friends on projects like “aywy” and Digital Domain.
# meta::summary5 = (human5) Creators of Heaven Sent Gaming Mario and Isabel discuss how they met, the creation of their content from comics illustrated and written for class projects in college, and how the purpose behind their venture is to inspire people in the entertainment industry.
# meta::summaryClosed1 = (humanC1) Mario Lucero and Isabel Ruiz discuss the origin of their entertainment company, Heaven Sent Games, explaining how they met in high school and cultivated a creative partnership throughout college, with Isabel illustrating stories Mario had written and both having the same creative vision of media they wanted to produce.
# meta::summaryClosed2 = (humanC2) This interview focuses on subjects Mario Lucero and Isabel Ruiz, who, after becoming friends in high school and throughout college, founded the entertainment collective Heaven Sent Gaming, and generate content that combines Isabel's drawings and sketches with Mario's writing, as well as other content sprouting from college projects and collaborations with friends.
