# meta::salientEntities = 1 (5*), 3 (5*), 12 (5*), 4 (4*), 8 (4), 44 (4*), 2 (3), 11 (3*), 47 (3*), 26 (2*), 35 (2*), 101 (2*), 104 (2), 15 (1), 17 (1), 18 (1), 19 (1*), 20 (1), 22 (1*), 23 (1*), 27 (1), 28 (1), 31 (1*), 36 (1), 59 (1*), 60 (1*), 70 (1), 76 (1*)
# meta::sourceURL = https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Coron
# meta::speakerCount = 0
# meta::summary1 = (human1) This overview of the history of Coron, a fishing town on the island of Busuanga in the Philippines, tells about the local people (Tagbanuas), the shift from farming to mining, fishing, and more recently tourism, and attractions such as stunning lakes, snorkeling, and wreck diving to see around ten Japanese ships sunk by the US Navy in World War II.
# meta::summary2 = (human2) Coron is a small fishing town in Palawan, Philippines that became famous (recognized as a top diving spot) in the tourism industry for its well-preserved underwater Japanese shipwrecks from World War II and other attractions managed and protected by an indigenous tribe.
# meta::summary3 = (human3) Coron is the largest town on the island Busuanga in the Philippines that is primarily inhabited by the indigenous Tagbanuas, and is famous for its WWII wreck diving, where tourists can see the wrecks of 10 Japanese ships that were sunk by American warplanes in September 1944.
# meta::summary4 = (human4) Coron, the largest town on Busuanga Island in the Palawan province of the Philippines, is the ancestral home of the Tagbanuas, an indigenous tribe of nomadic, seafaring people, but it is now better known as a tourist destination famous for its World War II wreck diving, white sand beaches, and ideal locations for snorkeling and scuba diving.
# meta::summary5 = (human5) Coron, a small quaint fishing town on Busuanga Island in Palawan, Philippines, known for its WWII shipwrecks and natural attractions, has evolved from a Tagbanua-inhabited fishing village to a booming tourist destination focused on scuba diving and history.
# meta::summaryClosed1 = (humanC1) Coron is a municipality of the Philippines, originally occupied by an indigenous Indonesian tribe, which has experienced industry booms of mining and fishing in the last century and currently boasts one of the best diving sites in the world due to the number of WWII ships that sank intact off its shore.
# meta::summaryClosed2 = (humanC2) The guide introduces an island Coron, which stresses the historical development from an unfamous island, where most inhabitants are indigenous, to an official town, and at last, becoming a famous touristic place for diving and fishing.
# meta::title = Coron
